{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100298","id":2230444222,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6E8eC-","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100298","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100298.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100298.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100298","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100298/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100298/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100298/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/92d533e1a74983e6070e257a0988f3c38db6072b","number":100298,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add builtin icons as a fallback option and as a way to use the editor's icons","user":{"login":"sylbeth","id":102521501,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhxanQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102521501?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth","html_url":"https://github.com/sylbeth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This check makes it so, in case any custom icon finding or opening were to fail, it fallbacks on a builtin icon in the theme with the same name. This way, we can specify an icon that's already in the engine instead of having to provide it. For example, if you wanted your CustomNode icon to be that of a CharacterBody2D, you could specify it as a path with \"CharacterBody2D\".\r\n\r\nThis would palliate the need to automatically find the base class to use as the icon. Not only that, but it also covers more use cases. Let's say you make a node that's akin to a person, but you use Node2D as the base instead. You could specify the icon to be that of CharacterBody2D instead.\r\n\r\nThis allows users not to have to provide the icon, saving space on the computer and also stopping them from bloating the project folders.\r\n\r\nIn this implementation though, worst case scenario the GDExtension::get_singleton()->class_get_icon_path(p_class) gets called twice, but this can easily be changed if that's what's wanted here, and I can change it myself.\r\n\r\nOriginal proposal: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11336\r\n\r\n(and already ran the pre-commit run)\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, closes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11336*","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":580537003,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODA1MzcwMDM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdextension","name":"topic:gdextension","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url